P18-V01 public-executor shutdown boundary —
2026-10-22 22:03 UTC

Environment: macOS AArch64, Rust 1.85.0. Branch:
`phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`. Java reference is RocketMQ 5.5.1,
commit `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.

Source comparison:
- Java `NettyRemotingClient.shutdown()` waits for `NettyEventExecutor.shutdown()`
  to join its worker for up to 90 seconds, then shuts down `publicExecutor`
  without waiting for its queued or running work.
- Rust had closed public-executor admission at shutdown initiation, before its
  channel-event worker join completed.

Correction, commit `dc625424`:
- Keep public-executor admission open through the channel-event worker join,
  then close admission when the worker stops or the join deadline expires.
- Apply the same boundary in foreground and cancellation-safe background
  cleanup. Accepted work continues to drain independently.
- Extend `shutdown_waits_for_channel_event_worker_only_until_java_join_limit`
  to prove a submission during the wait is accepted, a new submission after
  shutdown returns is rejected, and accepted work still completes.
- Refresh the Phase 3 Remoting inventory, Phase 16 channel-event matrix and
  `KNOWN_DIFFERENCES.md` lifecycle mapping.

Current-revision verification:
- Focused shutdown boundary regression — PASS.
- `cargo test --offline -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --lib --locked` — PASS
  (140 tests).
- `cargo test --offline -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --test transport --locked`
  — PASS (107 tests).
- Strict all-target/all-feature Remoting Clippy — PASS.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` — PASS.

Broad P18-V01 source/API/settings/input/error/control-flow and reverse-export
reconciliation remains open. No external CI, push, publication, or release
